    "title": "043: The Knowledge Window, Round 2: a Plain Search Page, a Best Match, and a Corpus That Grows"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 2354,
      "end_line": 26,
      "line": 22,
      "start": 1396
    },
    "text": "The archives pane is how the operator reads what Delphi knows. Round 2 does four things:\n1. **A plain page.** A search box in the middle and nothing else, as the early search engines did. No chat prompt on this pane; the footer stays.\n2. **A results page that is easy to scan.** One **best match** with a short summary of itself, then a uniform list. Everything that costs tokens is a separate, labelled, opt-in action.\n3. **Two new first-class kinds, `research` and `docs`,** so the corpus that expand mode pulls down (028-A1) and the operator's own reference documents are found, filtered and read like the specs and lessons.\n4. **A corpus that gets better with use.** Expand mode stores human-readable markdown; the more of it there is, the better both the search and the model summary (§8) become. This spec makes that growth visible (counts per kind, a one-key path from \"nothing here\" to \"research this\") but does not change how the job runs (028-A1)."
  }
